# Branches the push guard (~/.claude/hooks/guard-push.sh) refuses to push to.
# One name per line. Without this file the guard defaults to main and master;
# an empty list protects nothing.
#
# **Deliberately empty.** Profile: personal — the agent merges `main` itself
# once the gate passes, so a protected `main` here blocks the intended
# workflow rather than guarding anything.
#
# A personal template repo. CI runs on push to main, which is the signal; there is no deploy to gate.
#
# Added 2026-09-07. This repo was one of three personal repos still defaulting
# to a protected `main` because it never got an opt-out file, while tea,
# currant and second-brain had one. That inconsistency is what made "agents
# keep getting blocked pushing to main" feel intermittent and unexplainable.
#
# What still guards `main` without a PR: `git push --force`, `git push -f`,
# `git reset --hard` and `git clean -f` are denied globally, `origin` is a
# full second copy, and `git reflog` recovers a bad push.
#
# The file must EXIST and list nothing. Don't "tidy it up" by deleting it.
